{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,1]],"date-time":"2022-04-01T17:56:00Z","timestamp":1648835760768},"reference-count":25,"publisher":"World Scientific Pub Co Pte Lt","issue":"07","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Int. J. Mod. Phys. B"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2015,3,20]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> We develop entanglement perturbation theory (EPT) for infinite Quasi-1D quantum systems. The spin-1/2 Heisenberg chain with ferromagnetic nearest neighbor (NN) and antiferromagnetic next nearest neighbor (NNN) interactions with an easy-plane anisotropy is studied as a prototypical system. The obtained phase diagram is compared with a recent prediction [Phys. Rev. B 81, 094430 (2010)] that dimer and Néel orders appear alternately as the XXZ anisotropy Δ approaches the isotropic limit Δ = 1. The first and second transitions (across dimer, Néel and dimer phases) are detected with improved accuracy at Δ ≈ 0.722 and 0.930. The third transition (from dimer to Néel phases), previously predicted to be at Δ ≈ 0.98, is not detected at this Δ in our method, strongly indicating that the second Néel phase is absent. </jats:p>","DOI":"10.1142/s0217979215500423","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2014,12,31]],"date-time":"2014-12-31T03:33:46Z","timestamp":1419996826000},"page":"1550042","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Entanglement perturbation theory for infinite quasi-1D quantum systems"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"29","author":[{"given":"Lihua","family":"Wang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Computational Condensed-Matter Physics Laboratory, RIKEN, Wako, Saitama 351-0198, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Sung Gong","family":"Chung","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Physics and Nanotechnology Research and Computation Center, Western Michigan University, Kalamazoo, Michigan 49008, USA"},{"name":"Asia Pacific Center for Theoretical Physics, Pohang, Gyeonbuk 790-784, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"219","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2015,3,2]]},"reference":[{"key":"rf1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103/PhysRevB.81.094430"},{"key":"rf2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103/PhysRevB.25.4925"},{"key":"rf3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016/0375-9601(92)90823-5"},{"key":"rf4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088/0305-4470/28/19/003"},{"key":"rf5","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103/PhysRevLett.98.070201"},{"key":"rf6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103/PhysRevB.48.10345"},{"key":"rf7","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063/1.1664979"},{"key":"rf8","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103/PhysRevB.54.9862"},{"key":"rf10","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016/j.physleta.2006.07.025"},{"key":"rf11","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016/j.physleta.2006.09.057"},{"key":"rf12","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016/j.physleta.2008.04.067"},{"key":"rf13","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016/j.physleta.2009.04.038"},{"key":"rf14","volume-title":"Entanglement Perturbation Theory for Antiferromagnetic Spin Chains","author":"Wang L.","year":"2011"},{"key":"rf15","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1143/JPSJ.81.114712"},{"key":"rf16","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088/0305-4470/31/20/002"},{"key":"rf17","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103/PhysRevB.39.2562"},{"key":"rf18","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103/PhysRevB.69.064427"},{"key":"rf19","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103/PhysRevB.55.2164"},{"key":"rf20","first-page":"401","volume":"7","author":"Perez-Garcia D.","year":"2007","journal-title":"Quantum Inf. Comput."},{"key":"rf21","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088/1367-2630/12/2/025005"},{"key":"rf22","doi-asserted-by":"pu